  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is implicated in the target pathway leading to Peptide deformylase through multiple distinct mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Phellandral, (R)- acts as a target for CDK3/Cyclin E, which in turn is targeted by 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid, and also by Cornuside. Additionally, Phellandral, (R)- is linked to CDK3/Cyclin E, which is targeted by a complex compound with a unique structural profile. These findings collectively indicate that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its biological effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Peptide deformylase. The presence of multiple targets and their respective pathways suggests that Phellandral, (R)- may act as a modulator of the metabolic processes involving Peptide deformylase, potentially through a mechanism that involves the regulation of cyclin-dependent kinases and their associated targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Phellandral, (R)- and Peptide deformylase, emphasizing the role of CDK3/Cyclin E in mediating this interaction.",
